      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s wording is more general than what the packet explicitly supports: it describes family studies as comparing “people with a condition” to infer whether a “trait or difficulty” reflects shared susceptibility, whereas the packet specifically frames a family study to clarify whether *decision-making deficits* (poor performance on lab decision-making paradigms) may have predated heroin use due to familial susceptibility versus emerging as a consequence of chronic drug use.",
        "Because the packet only provides a concrete example involving heroin dependence and siblings, the definition’s broader phrasing (“trait or difficulty”) is an unsupported generalization beyond the provided text."
